   "id": "bb-021-comp",
   "h": "Appropriate compensation",
   "html": "<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Appropriate compensation</th><th>Ratio (CO<sub>2</sub>:HCO<sub>3</sub><sup>−</sup>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Metabolic Acidosis</td><td>12:10</td></tr><tr><td>Metabolic Alkalosis</td><td>7:10</td></tr><tr><td>Acute Respiratory Acidosis</td><td>10:1</td></tr><tr><td>Chronic Respiratory Acidosis</td><td>10:3</td></tr><tr><td>Acute Respiratory Alkalosis</td><td>10:2</td></tr><tr><td>Chronic Respiratory Alkalosis</td><td>10:4</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "bb-021-types",
   "h": "Classification by pH and ventilation",
   "html": "<ul><li><b>pH &lt; 7.35 (Acidemia)</b>: Metabolic Acidosis — Elevated Anion Gap (see “Metabolic Acidosis Elevated Anion Gap” on page 119), Normal Anion Gap (see “Metabolic Acidosis Normal Anion Gap” on page 118); Respiratory Acidosis — Chronic (hypoventilation present for hours to days), Acute (hypoventilation present for minutes to hours)</li><li><b>pH 7.35–7.45 (Normal pH)</b>: Mixed Acid-Base Disorder</li><li><b>pH &gt; 7.45 (Alkalemia)</b>: Metabolic Alkalosis (see “Metabolic Alkalosis” on page 117); Respiratory Alkalosis — Chronic (hyperventilation present for hours to days), Acute (hyperventilation present for minutes to hours)</li></ul>"
  }
 ],
